Your current behavior is partially correct, but I recommend implementing synchronization for the Next Round and final-score actions too.

The reason is that `/guess` is a server request, so it can broadcast an SSE event. However, `continueGame()` currently only changes Angular state locally. The server never knows that one tab pressed “Next Round.”

Also, SSE is one-way. The button must make an HTTP request first; the server can then broadcast the resulting state to all tabs.

