After these changes:

1. Tab A submits a guess.
2. Both tabs show the round result.
3. Tab A presses “Next Round.”
4. Tab A calls the new `/advance` endpoint.
5. The server broadcasts `game.round-advanced`.
6. Both tabs display the next round.
7. On round three, Tab A presses “See Final Score.”
8. The score route broadcasts `game.completed`.
9. Both tabs show the final-score screen.

So, while your current behavior is acceptable as a partial demonstration, synchronizing these transitions is better if you want to claim that the game state is genuinely real-time across tabs.
